paper/src/main.tex:333:Hence, the $\hbar$-perfectness of $G_1$ and $G_2$ leads to the $\hbar$-perfectness of $G$.
paper/src/main.tex:336:    If $G_1, G_2$ are $\hbar$-perfect and $G$ is the fully disconnected disjoint union of $G_1$ and $G_2$, then $G$ is also $\hbar$-perfect.
paper/src/main.tex:341:    For an $\hbar$-perfect graph $G$, if $G'$ is an induced subgraph of $G$ with the vertex set $V'$, then $G'$ is also $\hbar$-perfect.
