paper/src/main.tex:536:Due to the fact that we optimize in the Bose symmetric subspace, we can use a finite de Finetti theorem customized for this.
paper/src/main.tex:537:From the finite de Finetti theorem~\cite[Thm.~II.8]{Christandl2007}, it is guaranteed that there exists a separable bipartite state $\tau$ such that the trace distance $T(\tau,\tr_m \sigma) \le 4d/(m+2)$ .
paper/src/main.tex:552:To have the difference between $\lambda_{\max}(H_S^{(m)})$ and $\beta(G,w)$ smaller than $\epsilon > 0$, it suffices to set $m = O(nd/\epsilon)$. Consequently, $D = O((nd/\epsilon)^d)$ and the runtime of the whole algorithm is $O((nd/\epsilon)^{3d})$.
paper/src/main.tex:553:Since this hierarchy is polynomial in $n$ and superexponential in $d$, it is suitable for large graphs represented by short Pauli strings of length $\ell$.
paper/src/main.tex:554:Nevertheless, the number of nontrivial Pauli strings with length $\ell$ is $4^\ell - 1$, which is the maximal size of the corresponding frustration graph.
