paper/src/main.tex:580:\section{\texorpdfstring{Frequency of $\mathbf{\hbar}$-perfectness}{}}
paper/src/main.tex:582:Having introduced the properties and numerical tools, an immediate question to ask is: How common are $\hbar$-perfect graphs? 
paper/src/main.tex:584:As it turns out, small graphs can be tested for $\hbar$-perfectness and $\hbar$-imperfectness quite efficiently. 
paper/src/main.tex:586:To determine whether an $h$-imperfect graph is $\hbar$-perfect, we have first made use of the aforementioned properties. For the undetermined ones, we have employed the numerical methods in the previous section for the estimation. 
paper/src/main.tex:587:Then the $\hbar$-perfectness and $\hbar$-imperfectness of all graphs with $8$ vertices are determined up to a precision of $1\times 10^{-5}$. Among all connected graphs with $9$ vertices, only $78$ of them are left undetermined. 
