paper/src/main.tex:679:The detection of entanglement reduces to the separation of a point from a polytope, for which there are more economic algorithms, such as the Gilbert algorithm. In addition, we can use the symmetry of the graph $G$ to further reduce the complexity of the algorithm as in Ref.~\cite{xu2023graph}.
