The paper’s own shortcut is already visible: Appendix A.3 / the dense-encoding theorem identifies the minimum Pauli-string realization length with half the adjacency matrix’s rank over \(\mathbb F_2\), and the paper says the standard realization attains it. That immediately rules out a Track A claim for “find the minimum length”—Gaussian elimination/symplectic factorization is the certificate-producing algorithm. I’m checking whether there is a legitimate Track B gap (large exact elimination versus a short structural rank/kernel witness) before accepting or rejecting that direction; I’m also checking the weighted-independent-set route against the paper’s easy regimes and exact algorithms.
