The native generator now passes G1–G8 in preflight. At the shipping preset it samples 200,000 structure-valid nonzero bit vectors with 0 hits; the exact kernel density is about \(7.82\times10^{-149}\). All five no-tool attacks fail on 8/8 seeds, while the explicitly disclosed reference polynomial-gcd algorithm solves 8/8, averaging about 59,700 GF(2) coefficient XORs. The answer is 173 characters / 3 atoms, and the compact motif-and-quotient route measures 289 exact operations, just under the 300-operation cap. Next I’m running the mandated independent oracle ladder, then the structural and placebo arms in isolated directories.
