The bare run produced valid evidence that the old easy rung was too easy (2 of 3 vendors solved it), then the OpenRouter account hit its total key limit before medium could be tested. The harness correctly aborted rather than recording API exhaustion as model failure. I’m using that real result to remove the weak rung and, while the oracle budget is unavailable, tightening answer diversity: the reciprocal factor will now vary with the seed, so shipping instances do not all share one planted kernel vector.
